  "//": "Every literal the Phase 2 token sweep left behind, and nothing else.\n\nThis is a ratchet, not an exemption list. scripts/css-token-sweep.test.mjs\ncompares it against the tree with a set equality, so a literal that is not\nrecorded here fails the build and a recorded literal that has been migrated\nfails it too. Adding a row is therefore a deliberate act with a reviewer,\nwhich is the only property that makes a debt list shrink instead of drift.\n\nRows are grouped by file and property and hold the declaration value, not a\nline number: two rules that paint the same literal share one row, and\nediting anything above a rule does not churn the ledger.\n\nWhy each row is still here is answered by role, not one row at a time: the\n'Role gaps' table in docs/theming.md groups every colour below under the\ntier-2 role that would absorb it, and the 'Replaces' tables under 'Scales'\ncover the rest -- most scale rows are values whose nearest step would move a\npixel, which is a design decision rather than a substitution.\n\nA literal a token already spells exactly is a plain miss and not debt at\nall. The sweep test judges those separately and that list is empty: every\nexact match has been substituted, so nothing below can be removed without\nchoosing a different colour or moving a box.",
